   "source": [
    "# VIVO Backgammon — ENTRENAMIENTO GRANDE (self-play rápido)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Qué hace este notebook:** entrena la red neuronal (198→256→128→64→1) por **self-play** (la IA juega contra sí misma) usando un motor NumPy que replica EXACTAMENTE las reglas del navegador. Así escala a decenas/millones de partidas sin el cuello de botella de la heurística.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Pasos para ti (Thomas):**\n",
    "1. Sube `bg_fast.py`, `bg_train_fast.py` y este notebook a Kaggle (o impórtalos desde el repo `Pirzl/Backgammon-AR-Pro` rama `260816-gpu-train`).\n",
    "2. **Engranaje ⚙️ → Accelerator = GPU P100** (NO None) y **Internet = ON**. Save.\n",
    "3. **Run → Run All**.\n",
    "4. Al terminar, descarga `public/model_weights.json` y súbelo a InfinityFree (dentro de `dist/`).\n",
    "\n",
    "El modelo de salida es compatible con el navegador tal cual (mismo formato que `bg_net.py`)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Celda 0 — descarga el motor rápido y el trainer del repo (rama 260816-gpu-train)\n",
    "import urllib.request, os\n",
    "base = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Pirzl/Backgammon-AR-Pro/260816-gpu-train/colab/'\n",
    "for f in ['bg_engine.py', 'bg_fast.py', 'bg_train_fast.py', 'parity_test.py']:"
    "    if not os.path.exists(f):\n",
    "        urllib.request.urlretrieve(base + f, f)\n",
    "        print('descargado', f)\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print('ya existe', f)\n",
    "\n",
    "import tensorflow as tf\n",
    "gpus = tf.config.list_physical_devices('GPU')\n",
    "print('GPU disponible:', gpus)\n",
    "if not gpus:\n",
    "    print('AVISO: no hay GPU -> sera lento (CPU). Cambia Accelerator a GPU P100 en el engranaje.')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('OK: entrenamiento en GPU.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Celda 1 — VEREDICTO de sanity (opcional): confirma que el motor rápido\n",
    "# coincide con el motor lento del navegador.\n",
    "import subprocess\n",
    "r = subprocess.run(['python', 'parity_test.py'], capture_output=True, text=True)\n",
    "print(r.stdout)\n",
    "print(r.stderr[-500:] if r.stderr else '')\n",
    "assert 'PARITY OK' in r.stdout, 'PARIDAD FALLÓ — no entrenes.'"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Celda 2 — ENTRENAMIENTO GRANDE (self-play)\n",
    "# Ajusta --games al tamaño que quieras. Guía:\n",
    "#   20k  -> ~15 min GPU, notable mejora sobre 300\n",
    "#   100k -> ~1h GPU, nivel fuerte\n",
    "#   500k -> varias horas, cerca de maestro (Tesauro usó 1.5M+)\n",
    "#\n",
    "# Para REANUDAR desde tu modelo de 300 partidas, descomenta la línea --weights.\n",
    "# (Sube model_weights.json de 300 como input de datos en Kaggle y pon la ruta.)\n",
    "\n",
    "games = 100000          # <-- cambia aquí el tamaño del entrenamiento\n",
    "exploration = 0.15      # exploración (TD-Gammon clásico ~0.1-0.2)\n",
    "max_moves = 400\n",
    "epochs = 3\n",
    "save_every = 10000      # guarda cada N partidas (checkpoint + descarga parcial)\n",
    "seed = 1\n",
    "\n",
    "# Para reanudar desde el modelo de 300 partidas, descomenta y ajusta la ruta:\n",
    "# weights_arg = '--weights /kaggle/input/TU_INPUT/model_weights.json'\n",
    "weights_arg = ''\n",
    "\n",
    "cmd = (\n",
    "    f'python bg_train_fast.py --games {games} '\n",
    "    f'--exploration {exploration} --max-moves {max_moves} '\n",
    "    f'--epochs {epochs} --save-every {save_every} '\n",
    "    f'--out public/model_weights.json --seed {seed} {weights_arg}'\n",
    ")\n",
    "print('Ejecutando:', cmd)\n",
    "import subprocess\n",
    "r = subprocess.run(cmd, shell=True)\n",
    "print('exit code:', r.returncode)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Celda 3 — Verifica y descarga el modelo\n",
    "import os, json\n",
    "p = 'public/model_weights.json'\n",
    "assert os.path.exists(p), 'No se generó model_weights.json'\n",
    "w = json.load(open(p))\n",
    "print('Capas:', len(w))\n",
    "print('Formas:', [l['shape'] for l in w])\n",
    "print('Tamaño:', round(os.path.getsize(p)/1024/1024, 2), 'MB')\n",
    "print('LISTO: descarga public/model_weights.json y súbelo a InfinityFree en dist/')"
   ]
  }
